    'bgsAdmin.emptyLoading': 'Loading state…',
    'bgsAdmin.interrupted': 'The previous load was cut short together with the site process (update or restart). What was downloaded and split stays on the server — “Load now” continues from the same point (already written chunks are not rewritten); the factions-sync task does this by itself on its next run.',
    'bgsAdmin.noteSourceLead': 'Source:',
    'bgsAdmin.noteSourceBody': '— the nightly EDSM dump: every populated system with its minor factions (influence, states), ≈0.5 GB gzip. The archive is downloaded to the server in full over {connections} connections (FACTIONS_DOWNLOAD_SEGMENTS), with file chunks of {mb} MB; a drop or site restart keeps what was downloaded. A connection silent for {stall} s (FACTIONS_STALL_SECONDS) reconnects at once instead of waiting the 70 s OS timeout.',
    'bgsAdmin.noteShortOff': ' Short requests are off (FACTIONS_REQUEST_KB=off).',
    'bgsAdmin.noteShortNumber': ' Requests fetch {size} each in a new connection (FACTIONS_REQUEST_KB).',
    'bgsAdmin.noteShortAuto': ' If connections stall after transferring only a few kilobytes (server networks cut sessions to foreign CDNs, and EDSM sits behind Cloudflare), the load switches by itself to short requests below that threshold, each in a new connection.',
    'bgsAdmin.noteSplit': 'Once the archive is downloaded it is split into chunks of {count} systems (stations and bodies are dropped — megabytes remain of 0.5 GB), then the chunks are written to the database; a chunk is the unit of resumption. If EDSM rebuilds the dump mid-download (around 04:50 UTC), the download restarts with the fresh dump — halves of two dumps are never glued together. After a successful load the archive and chunks',
    'bgsAdmin.noteKeepArchive': ' stay on the server (FACTIONS_ARCHIVE_KEEP=1)',
    'bgsAdmin.noteKeepDelete': ' are deleted from the server',
    'bgsAdmin.noteFresh': 'Fresher observations win: systems that pilots reported after the dump date are left alone by the import. Systems missing from the dump are deleted only if pilots have not reported them for {days} days. Guard: with fewer than {min} systems or a dump smaller than half of the previous one, missing systems are not deleted.',
    'bgsAdmin.noteSchedule': 'Automatically: the factions-sync task once a day{next} refreshes data older than {days} days (FACTIONS_REFRESH_DAYS) and continues an interrupted import; the first import only from here.',
    'bgsAdmin.noteScheduleNext': ' (next run — {when})',
